note neighbours.om: put on a bool field must not touch the fields around it, and a put on a
note neighbour must not touch the bool. Fields a=11 f=true b=22 g=false c=33; f is put false,
note g is put true. Bits: f false 1, g true 2, a+b+c = 66 (total 69). Then a b c become 1 2 3:
note f false 4, g true 8, a+b+c = 6. Result 69 + 12 + 6 = 87.
struct N a uint f bool b uint g bool c uchar end
fn main to uint
n = new N 11 true 22 false 33
put n f false
put n g true
r = uint 0
if eq get n f false
r = add r 1
end
if eq get n g true
r = add r 2
end
r = add r get n a
r = add r get n b
r = add r uint get n c
put n a 1
put n b 2
put n c 3
if eq get n f false
r = add r 4
end
if eq get n g true
r = add r 8
end
r = add r get n a
r = add r get n b
r = add r uint get n c
ret r
end
